<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue library="true" id="efa0-300e-3f94-8853" name="aLib - Apocalypse" gameSystemId="sys-86a7-ff6f-05e6-a304" gameSystemRevision="14" revision="2" battleScribeVersion="2.03" type="catalogue" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" publicationId="ef2a-0b23-f995-b91e">
  <publications>
    <publication id="ef2a-0b23-f995-b91e" name="Army - Apocalypse(1).docx" hidden="false"/>
  </publications>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink type="catalogue" name="aLib - Imperial - Base" targetId="0d98-1036-43bc-85f0" importRootEntries="false" id="1b30-dec3-b5d7-e3c9"/>
  </catalogueLinks>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Penetrating (+X)" hidden="false" id="eebe-5a41-8756-7b0b">
      <description>If the weapon scores any unsaved wounds, before Feel No Pain, as well as applying penetrating, add X points of damage.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Void Shields" hidden="false" id="c166-c9f9-2faf-37f6">
      <description>Void shields count as a Mechanical model added to a Titanic model’s unit, with AV13, W1, Sv 5++. Ranged attacks automatically target any remaining Void Shields before they target the Titanic model.
Void Shields are ignored for melee attacks.
When the Titanic model is destroyed, its Void Shields are also destroyed. The Sniper rule cannot target individual Void Shields or the Titanic model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hover Mode" hidden="false" id="e7f1-3cfa-6752-f655">
      <description>In the Command Phase, this model can choose to convert between Aircraft and Tank | Hover.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Beam" hidden="false" id="911a-e9b0-76ec-57d8">
      <description>Draw a straight line from the model out to the full range of the weapon. Its range is reduced by terrain as per other weapons. If the range would be reduced such that it does not reach the terrain, then the beam instead extends to the edge of the terrain. Each unit (friend or foe) that the beam passes over is hit, and must be attacked as though it were the target of a ranged attack. The beam is subject to the Split Fire rules: it must be directed such that it hits at least one of the targeted units that the model nominates.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lifta-Droppa" hidden="false" id="42ff-48de-2508-681f">
      <description>Instead of rolling to hit and wound, instead roll 2d6 and compare to the Strength of the target. If the value exceeds the Strength, the target suffers a wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psycho-dakka-blasta" hidden="false" id="8ca6-5b71-5f6d-2ed7">
      <description>After firing all of the unit’s weapons, if you fired the Supa-gatler, you can choose to fire it again immediately. Roll a d6: On a 1, the gun jams and cannot be used for the rest of the battle. On a 2+, declare a new target that the Supa-gatler has not shot at this turn and resolve the Supa-gatler’s shots at that same target. You can use this rule as many times as you like in a round, but you subtract an additional 1 from the roll each subsequent time you do so.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
